The Emails module in Taskip provides a centralized interface to manage all email communications within your workspace. It allows users to send, receive, organize, and track emails efficiently without leaving the platform.

## Email Interface Layout

The Emails module is divided into three main sections:

### Sidebar (Folders)

Located on the left side, it contains all email categories:

- **Inbox** – All received emails
- **Sent** – Emails you have sent
- **Drafts** – Saved but not sent emails
- **Outbox** – Emails queued for sending
- **Archive** – Stored emails for long-term keeping
- **Trash** – Deleted emails
- **Spam** – Filtered unwanted emails

### Email List Panel

Displays emails based on the selected folder.

#### Features:

- **Search Bar** – Search emails by keyword
- **Filter Option** – Apply filters to refine results
- **Tabs:**
  - All
  - Read
  - Unread

#### Empty State:

If no emails exist, the system shows:

> “Your inbox is empty”

### Email Detail View

The right panel displays the selected email.

#### Default State:

If no email is selected:

> “No email selected”

#### When Selected:

You can:

- View full email content
- Reply to email
- Manage attachments

## Compose Email

### Description

Allows you to create and send a new email.

### How to Use

1. Click **Compose** button
1. Enter:
   - Recipient email
   - Subject
   - Message content
1. Attach files (optional)
1. Click **Send**

## Email Status Types

- **Read** – Email has been opened
- **Unread** – Email not opened yet
- **Sent** – Successfully delivered
- **Draft** – Saved but not sent

## Email Actions

Users can perform the following actions:

- Read email
- Reply to email
- Delete email
- Archive email
- Mark as read/unread
- Move between folders

## Search and Filter

### Search

- Search emails using keywords

### Filter

- Filter by:
  - Read
  - Unread
  - All emails

## System Behavior

- Emails are categorized automatically into folders
- Drafts are saved until sent or deleted
- Deleted emails move to Trash
- Spam emails are filtered automatically
- Email details load when selected

## Use Cases

- Manage client communication
- Track conversations
- Handle support queries
- Organize internal email workflows

## Summary

The Emails module in Taskip provides a simple yet powerful way to manage all email communications. With organized folders, search and filter options, and a clean interface, it ensures efficient communication and better workflow management within your workspace.
